{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Reapertips ReaScripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Free scripts for REAPER by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reapertips.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Reapertips
}}}
 \u55357 ?\u56473 ?\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 \u55357 ?\u56550 ? Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 In REAPER, go to {\f1 Extensions} > {\f1 ReaPack} > {\f1 Import repositories...} and paste this:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/Reapertips/ReaScripts/raw/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Then go to {\f1 Extensions} > {\f1 ReaPack} > {\f1 Browse packages...} and install whatever you want!\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Don't have ReaPack yet? No worries! \u8211- here's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapertips.com/post/how-to-install-reapack"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
how to install it
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Packages\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55356 ?\u57272 ? TunerBox\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A chromatic tuner that lives right in your transport bar. Click the tuning fork to turn it on, click the readout for a big tuner window, and right click for options. It also remembers how you set it up for each theme.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This one needs the {\b js_ReaScriptAPI} extension. ReaPack will offer to install it for you.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55357 ?\u56628 ? Time selection color for loop and record\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Tints your time selection while Repeat/Loop is on, and again while REAPER is recording, so you can tell both states apart without looking away from what you're doing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each state decides on its own which areas it paints: arrange, MIDI editor, ruler, or the whole ruler strip as an adjustable tint. Colors are remembered per theme, and the settings window has a live preview.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Nothing extra to install, and colors are only changed in memory, so your theme file is never touched.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 License\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIT. Check {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "LICENSE"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
LICENSE
}}}
 for the third party notices.\par}
}
